<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ========================================================================
     DROIDWORKS_WILD_DROIDS_1 (packet E4). The wild-droid incident.

     Owner ruling 2 (design/Jawa/droids/DROID_UNIFIED_FRAMEWORK_DESIGN.md §0),
     verbatim: "there's the wild droids that have gone crazy from being left
     out in the desert after crashing" - and, in the same ruling, "NO rogue
     droid faction, ever". So this incident spawns a droid with NO faction at
     all, hostile through ManhunterPermanent rather than through a faction
     relation. That factionless state is the key RSW_DW_DataSpike_Wild
     (DataSpikes_Droidworks.xml, packet B3) was already cut for.

     ONE firing route, deliberately. DROID_REPAIR_FOR_PROFIT_EVENTS_1 (packet
     C5) established the engine constraint the hard way: IncidentDef's own
     ConfigErrors() forbids a def that is both selectable from the random
     incident pool (baseChance > 0 + targetTags) AND fired as a quest root.
     This one is a plain random incident and nothing else.

     workerClass: Source/Droidworks/IncidentWorker_WildDroidCrash.cs. Read its
     header before changing anything here - in particular why the count is
     exactly one droid (two factionless HUMANLIKE manhunters are force-hostile
     to each other and would fight instead of attacking) and why the pool is a
     flat weighted pick rather than points-scaled (every utility droid kind in
     this mod carries the combatPower 99999 "keep out of raid pools" sentinel).

     Frequency: baseChance 0.7 with minRefireDays 20. Chosen, not copied -
     Droidworks ships no other IncidentDef to mirror, and the nearest house
     precedent is RimStarWars' own RSW_WS_DarkAurora (baseChance 1.2,
     minRefireDays 15, IncidentDefs_DarkAurora.xml). Set below that on both
     axes because this one leaves a live hostile on the map with no timeout,
     and because §6's anti-exponential check caps the rate at which new droid
     bodies can enter the colony's economy: at ~20+ days apart a wild droid is
     an event, not a supply line.
======================================================================== -->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>RSW_DW_WildDroidCrash</defName>
    <label>wild droid</label>
    <description>A droid abandoned in the desert long enough to lose its mind wanders into the area. It belongs to nobody and is hostile to everybody.</description>
    <category>ThreatSmall</category>
    <baseChance>0.7</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>20</minRefireDays>
    <pointsScaleable>false</pointsScaleable>
    <letterDef>ThreatSmall</letterDef>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.IncidentWorker_WildDroidCrash</workerClass>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.WildDroidCrashExtension">
        <!-- Weighted by how plausibly the thing was left in a desert:
             abandoned labour and salvage units are commonest, old war
             leftovers next, one-off oddities rarest. Every defName here is
             a Droidworks kind (PawnKinds_*.xml in this mod), so the pool
             cannot break on a donor mod being retired under D2/D3/D4. -->
        <options>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_OuterRim_ImperialLaborDroid</kind><weight>10</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_OuterRim_SalvageAssistDroid</kind><weight>8</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_OuterRim_DUMDroid</kind><weight>6</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_OuterRim_RSeriesDroid</kind><weight>6</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_OuterRim_MuckrakerDroid</kind><weight>4</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_OuterRim_BattleDroid</kind><weight>10</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_JDSCIS_B1_Battle_Droid</kind><weight>10</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_JDSCIS_B1_Security_Droid</kind><weight>5</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_OuterRim_SuperBattleDroid</kind><weight>3</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_KM1MD</kind><weight>5</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_ADMkI</kind><weight>3</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_Primitive_G2</kind><weight>3</weight></li>
          <li><kind>RSW_DW_OuterRim_GNKDroid</kind><weight>2</weight></li>
        </options>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
